        wordCount: 520,
        readTime: "4 dk",
        text: `Once upon a time, there was a fast and proud Hare. He lived in a green forest with many animal friends. Every single morning, the Hare liked to run around the meadow. He ran very fast, jumping over rocks and streams with great energy.\n\nOne sunny afternoon, the Hare met a small Tortoise walking very slowly on the dirt path. The Tortoise moved with quiet steps, carrying his heavy green shell on his back. The Hare stopped and began to laugh loudly. "Look at you, my slow friend!" the Hare said with a big smile. "You take one tiny step every minute! I can run across the whole mountain while you only cross the river. You are the slowest animal in our whole land!"\n\nThe wise Tortoise stopped on the warm grass. He looked at the proud Hare with calm and gentle eyes. "Yes, Hare, you are indeed very fast," the Tortoise said softly. "You have long legs and light feet. But I can run a long race with you right now, and I believe I can win." The Hare laughed even harder. He fell on the soft green grass and laughed until tears ran from his eyes. "You beat me in a race? What a funny joke! Let us ask our forest friends to set the race today!"\n\nAll the animals gathered near the old oak tree. The wise Fox drew a long white line on the ground for the finish line at the far end of the valley. "Ready, steady, go!" shouted the Fox. The Hare ran forward like the wind. In only five seconds, he was far away at the top of the green hill. The Tortoise began to walk with slow, steady steps. Step by step, he moved forward without stopping.\n\nThe day was warm and the sun shone brightly in the blue sky. At the middle of the hill, the Hare looked back. He could not even see the slow Tortoise on the dusty path. "That funny creature is so far behind," the Hare thought to himself. "I have plenty of time. I will lie down under this cool shady tree and take a quick nap. Then I will wake up, run to the finish line, and win the race easily."\n\nSo the Hare closed his eyes under the cool tree and fell into a deep sleep. Meanwhile, the Tortoise kept walking. His small legs were tired, but his heart was patient. He did not stop to eat grass, and he did not sit down to rest. Hour after hour passed under the warm sun. Slowly and steadily, the Tortoise walked past the sleeping Hare under the tree.\n\nSuddenly, the Hare woke up. The sun was going down behind the mountains. The evening air was cool. The Hare jumped to his feet in panic and looked toward the finish line. To his great surprise, the Tortoise was just one step away from crossing the line! All the animals in the valley were cheering loudly: "Go, Tortoise, go!"\n\nThe Hare ran as fast as his legs could carry him, but it was too late. The slow Tortoise crossed the finish line first and won the race! The wise Fox smiled and said: "Slow and steady wins the race."`,
