        wordCount: 505,
        readTime: "4 dk",
        text: `There was once a young shepherd boy who watched over a flock of sheep on a peaceful hillside near a small village. The boy sat on the soft grass from morning until evening. Most of the time, the sheep grazed quietly, and nothing exciting ever happened. The boy grew very lonely and bored.\n\nOne afternoon, while watching the sheep eat grass, the boy thought of a clever trick to amuse himself. He climbed onto a large rock overlooking the valley, put his hands around his mouth, and shouted as loudly as he could: "Wolf! Wolf! A fierce wolf is attacking the sheep! Please come and help me!"\n\nDown in the village, the hardworking villagers heard his loud cries. They immediately dropped their farm tools, grabbed wooden sticks and pitchforks, and ran up the steep hill to save the sheep. When they arrived, panting and out of breath, they found no wolf at all. The sheep were calmly resting, and the young boy was rolling on the green grass, laughing hysterically at his foolish trick.\n\n"You should not joke about such serious danger, young boy!" warned an elderly villager angrily. "A wolf is no laughing matter." The villagers shook their heads in frustration and walked back down to their daily work.\n\nA few days later, the boy was bored once again. Even though he knew it was wrong, he climbed the rock and shouted with all his might: "Wolf! Wolf! Help, the wolf is here again!" Once more, the kind villagers rushed up the hillside to rescue him. When they arrived, the boy pointed at them and laughed even louder. The villagers were furious. "Nobody believes a liar, even when he tells the truth!" shouted a farmer before walking away.\n\nLater that evening, as the sun was setting behind the dark forest, a real and ferocious grey wolf crept out of the shadows. The hungry beast attacked the frightened sheep, snapping its sharp teeth. Terrified for his life, the young shepherd boy ran toward the village, screaming in genuine terror: "Wolf! Wolf! Please, I beg you, a real wolf is killing the flock! Help me!"\n\nDown in the village, the farmers heard his desperate screams, but they smiled and continued their dinner. "He is just trying to fool us for a third time," they said to each other. "We will not waste our energy running up that hill again."\n\nNobody came to help. The fierce wolf scattered the entire flock and carried away several sheep into the deep forest. As night fell, the tearful boy sat alone on the hill, realizing the bitter lesson: when liars finally speak the truth, no one is willing to listen.`,
