        wordCount: 515,
        readTime: "4 dk",
        text: `Once upon a time, there were four little rabbits. Their names were Flopsy, Mopsy, Cotton-tail, and Peter. They lived with their caring mother in a cozy sandbank, underneath the root of a very big fir tree.\n\nOne fresh morning, old Mrs. Rabbit took her wicker basket and her umbrella. She looked at her four children with loving eyes. "Now, my dear children," she said gently, "you may go down the green lane or play in the sunny fields. But whatever you do, do not go into Mr. McGregor's garden! Your poor father had an accident there; he was put in a pie by Mrs. McGregor. Run along, play nicely, and don't get into mischief. I am going to the baker's shop to buy brown bread and sweet buns."\n\nFlopsy, Mopsy, and Cotton-tail were good, obedient little bunnies. They took small baskets and walked politely down the lane to gather sweet black blackberries from the bushes.\n\nBut Peter was very naughty. As soon as his mother turned the corner, he ran straight toward Mr. McGregor's farm. He found a small opening at the bottom of the tall wooden gate and squeezed his little blue jacket underneath it! First, he ate some juicy green lettuces and sweet French beans. Then, he ate some small red radishes. His tummy became quite full and round.\n\nFeeling rather sick from eating too much vegetables, Peter decided to search for some fresh parsley to calm his stomach. He hopped around the corner of a green cucumber frame. But suddenly, whom should he meet but Mr. McGregor himself!\n\nMr. McGregor was on his hands and knees planting young cabbages in the soft dirt. When he saw the little rabbit eating his vegetables, he jumped up with a loud shout. Waving a heavy wooden rake in the air, he ran after Peter, calling out: "Stop thief! Stop thief!"\n\nPeter was terribly frightened. He rushed all over the garden, for he had forgotten the way back to the wooden gate. He lost one of his blue shoes among the cabbages, and the other shoe among the potatoes. After losing them, he ran on all four legs and went much faster. Unfortunately, he ran right into a large gooseberry net and got caught by the large brass buttons on his brand-new blue jacket!`,
